    {
      "id": "block.absorbant",
      "className": "AbsorbantAbAttr",
      "label": "Leech Seed the target after my draining move",
      "summary": "After a draining move of mine hits, the target is planted with Leech Seed. My draining moves also heal 1.5 times as much (Drain Punch heals 50% more).",
      "tier": "C",
      "kind": "package",
      "status": "decomposed",
      "when": "event.after-my-hit",
      "whenLabel": "After my attack lands",
      "synonyms": [
        "leech seed",
        "draining move",
        "drain punch",
        "giga drain",
        "heal more from drain",
        "seed after drain",
        "absorb health"
      ],
      "examples": [
        "After Drain Punch hits, the target gets Leech Seed and Drain Punch heals 50% more"
      ],
      "params": [],
      "conditions": [],
      "guards": [],
      "feasibility": [
        "My move must be a draining move (one that heals me by a share of the damage it deals)",
        "The target must not be protected from added effects (like Shield Dust)",
        "The target must be able to receive Leech Seed (it is not Grass type and not already seeded)"
      ],
      "effect": {
        "id": "effect.package",
        "params": []
      },
      "reusableAlone": {
        "when": true,
        "if": true,
        "do": true
      },
      "packageReason": "Package, justified: the same class is read two ways (dispatched after my hit for the Leech Seed, and found BY NAME in HitHealAttr.getHealAmount for the x1.5 heal), and its draining-move test is a fixed closure of the parent class. Users: Absorbant (5161 attr 0), and two studio-built abilities that reuse the attr as a TRIGGER SOURCE (Extermination Vector 20003 attr 4, External Combustion 20018 attr 0): their instances are carriers whose canApply, apply and getCondition are replaced by the rule runtime (runtime-components.ts), so they are carried over unchanged by a rebuild and are not part of what this declaration rebuilds. Nothing to bind (no constructor closure). The by-name fire() scan is an engine call site, not a moment; it is recorded here and left untouched.",
      "uses": 3
    },
